    <section class="shell section--roomy">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <span class="num">02 / The collaboration</span>
        <div>
          <h2>A real client,<br />not a hypothetical brief.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-prose reveal" data-delay="1">
        <p>
          This project was developed in collaboration with <strong>MEC</strong> &mdash;
          allowing our team to work with a real organization rather than designing in
          isolation. We engaged with MEC stakeholders, explored current challenges around
          community engagement and events, and used those insights to shape a more
          grounded and realistic solution.
        </p>
        <p>
          Working directly with MEC helped ensure the project addressed real business and
          user needs, while giving our team experience designing within authentic
          organizational constraints. Unlike conceptual student projects, this work
          involved feedback and context from an established brand &mdash; balancing
          <strong>user needs, brand identity, feasibility, and business goals</strong>
          throughout the design process.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-showcase cs-showcase--two reveal" data-delay="2">
        <div class="cs-frame">
          <div class="cover-fill cover-mec" aria-hidden="true" style="opacity: 0.6;"></div>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 600 450" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"
               style="mix-blend-mode: multiply;">
            <g fill="oklch(28% 0.06 170)" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" opacity="0.8">
              <text x="40" y="60">TEAM &middot; MEC HQ &middot; VANCOUVER</text>
            </g>
          </svg>
          <img src="../assets/mec/02-team-mec-hq.jpg" alt="The team standing in front of the MEC sign at Mountain Equipment Company headquarters." onerror="this.style.display='none'">
          <span class="cs-frame__label">Team &middot; on-site at MEC HQ</span>
