    <section class="shell section--roomy">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <span class="num">03 / The problem</span>
        <div>
          <h2>A co-op that lost<br />its sense of community.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-prose reveal" data-delay="1">
        <p>
          MEC has a complicated story. Founded as a Canadian co-operative deeply rooted in
          environmental values and community, it was acquired by US-based Kingswood
          Capital in 2020 over loud member protest &mdash; then bought back by Canadian
          owners (3F Capital) in 2025. Three eras, two ruptures, and a lingering trust
          gap with the people who used to call MEC theirs.
        </p>
        <p>
          We interviewed eleven retail customers, store staff, and longtime members.
          Three patterns kept surfacing:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>A legacy trust gap.</strong> Long-time customers and ex-co-op
            members felt MEC had lost its mythology, its community, and its identity
            through the corporate years.</li>
          <li><strong>Difficulty for beginners.</strong> Newcomers felt overwhelmed and
            unsure where to begin or get guidance &mdash; despite MEC's reputation as a
            place that welcomes them.</li>
          <li><strong>A strong but hidden community.</strong> Loyal customers existed,
            but lacked visibility or any real way to connect with each other.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          A line from a MEC store staff member became our north star:
        </p>
        <p style="font-family: var(--display); font-size: var(--fs-h4); line-height: 1.25; color: var(--ink); max-width: 28ch; padding-left: var(--s-4); border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);">
          &ldquo;We host events to keep people connected. Community is a big part of
          what MEC stands for.&rdquo;
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="cs-image reveal" data-delay="2">
        <div class="cs-frame cs-frame--wide cs-frame--contain">
          <div class="cover-fill cover-mec" aria-hidden="true" style="opacity: 0.55;"></div>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 1600 900" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"
               style="mix-blend-mode: multiply;">
            <g fill="oklch(28% 0.06 170)" font-family="monospace" font-size="16" opacity="0.7">
              <text x="80" y="80">PROCESS DECK &middot; ETHNOGRAPHY &rarr; PROBLEM REFRAME</text>
            </g>
          </svg>
          <img src="../assets/mec/08-process-deck.png" alt="Composite of process deck slides showing ethnography, problem framing, and design exploration." onerror="this.style.display='none'">
          <span class="cs-frame__label">Process deck &middot; ethnography &rarr; reframe</span>
        </div>
        <p class="cs-image__caption">
          Excerpt from our process deck &middot; from early ethnography through reframing
          the problem space around community and trust.
        </p>
      </figure>
    </section>

