    <section class="shell section--roomy">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <span class="num">04 / Who we designed for</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Three people,<br />three reasons MEC matters.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-prose reveal" data-delay="1">
        <p>
          We developed personas and journeys around the people most affected by MEC's
          identity shift &mdash; <strong>George</strong>, a backcountry pro nostalgic
          for the co-op years; <strong>Piper</strong>, a sustainability-minded gear
          enthusiast searching for clear answers; and <strong>Spike</strong>, a newcomer
          to Vancouver who wanted to find his community through the outdoors.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="cs-image reveal" data-delay="2">
        <div class="cs-frame cs-frame--tall cs-frame--contain" style="max-width: 540px; margin: 0 auto;">
          <div class="cover-fill" aria-hidden="true" style="background: oklch(95% 0.02 90); opacity: 0.5;"></div>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 400 533" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"
               style="mix-blend-mode: multiply;">
            <g fill="oklch(28% 0.06 170)" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" opacity="0.7">
              <text x="32" y="44">PERSONA &middot; BACKCOUNTRY PRO &middot; GEORGE</text>
            </g>
          </svg>
          <img src="../assets/mec/04-persona-george.png" alt="Persona document — Backcountry Pro George, a mid-30s park ranger and longtime MEC customer." onerror="this.style.display='none'">
          <span class="cs-frame__label">Persona &middot; Backcountry Pro &middot; George</span>
        </div>
        <p class="cs-image__caption">
          One of three personas we developed. George represents the long-time member
          who watched MEC drift &mdash; and wants its community spirit back.
        </p>
      </figure>

      <figure class="cs-image reveal" data-delay="3">
