    <section class="shell section--roomy">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <span class="num">08 / Reflection</span>
        <div>
          <h2>What I took<br />from MEC.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-prose reveal" data-delay="1">
        <p style="font-size: var(--fs-lede); line-height: 1.45; color: var(--ink);">
          Designing alongside MEC showed me how product decisions become stronger when
          they are informed by real stakeholder context, not just assumptions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Working with a real client changed the way I prioritized. Every choice had to
          earn its place against MEC's brand identity, the team's feasibility, and the
          realities of how community actually forms around events. That pressure made
          the work better &mdash; and made me a sharper designer.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

